# Normalise line endings.
#
# Without this file the repository accumulated a mix of CRLF and LF in the
# index, which had three separate consequences:
#
#  1. Every Go file failed `gofmt -l`, so the standard Go CI check reported all
#     seven files as unformatted and printed whole-file diffs, burying any real
#     formatting signal.
#  2. The Java sender wrote lines with the platform separator, so a
#     Windows-hosted game server sent CRLF while the Go peer stripped only the
#     newline. A carriage return stayed welded to the final field and broke
#     every float parse on that host, silently, because the parse error was
#     discarded.
#  3. Identical commits produced different bytes on different machines, which
#     makes any build hash or artifact comparison meaningless.
#
# After adding this file, run once:
#     git add --renormalize .
# and commit the result on its own, so the mechanical churn does not
# contaminate every later diff.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.go    text eol=lf
*.java  text eol=lf
*.xml   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.mod   text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

*.jar   binary
*.class binary
*.png   binary
*.db    binary
